Let grid be a list of 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, and 0.
Let columns be 3.
Let size be the number of items in grid.
Let table be a list of size zeros.
For every position from 0 to one less than size.
Let row be position divided by columns.
Let column be position modulo columns.
If item position of grid is 1, set item position of table to 0.
If row is 0 and column is 0 and item position of grid is 0, set item position of table to 1.
If row is 0 and column is more than 0 and item position of grid is 0, set item position of table to item (position minus 1) of table.
If row is more than 0 and column is 0 and item position of grid is 0, set item position of table to item (position minus columns) of table.
If row is more than 0 and column is more than 0 and item position of grid is 0, set item position of table to item (position minus 1) of table plus item (position minus columns) of table.

Let last be one less than size.
Print item last of table.
